    "woodBoxAssessment": "Inspect low/mid peak distributions of wood-supported recording and other records. Wood resonances cannot be uniquely identified without dry/boxed paired recordings; room reverb, notes and mic coloration remain confounds. Keep prior subtle body filters, rather than copying a recorded resonance curve or claiming measured wood frequencies.",
    "designDecision": {
      "attack": "Keep existing1.2ms synthetic attack; single-note onset is about1ms or truncated, independent recordings are polyphonic and rise times not directly comparable.",
      "partials": "Dominant986/1478Hz tines differ in2f strength (about-17/-30dB). Independent instrument also has weaker2f around-23 to-29dB on several attacks. Reduce overly fixed upper inharmonic ringing slightly; retain tonal transparency.",
      "decay": "Single-note fitted dominant taus about.28/.81s differ greatly by tine. Do not force all notes to one decay constant. Keep fundamental envelopes and small deterministic differences; shorten upper-mode tails modestly.",
      "lowRegister": "Modest pitch-tapered2f/3f support is an engineering extrapolation for small speakers, NOT a directly measured real-instrument low register. Validate with band-limited model; human listening still required."
